    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the exact value of $\\sec\\theta$, given that $\\sin\\theta=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $\\theta\\in(270^{\\circ},360^{\\circ})$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}$",
      "worked": "The reference triangle has opposite side $2$ and hypotenuse $3$. By Pythagoras,\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\sqrt{3^2-2^2}\\\\a&=\\sqrt{5}\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is positive in quadrant IV.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\\\\\sec\\theta&=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\\\\\sec\\theta&=\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
